name c01m05-night-of-death
timeout 600
time 1992-10-29T10:21:00Z

# COMANCHE: MAXIMUM OVERKILL (NovaLogic 1992), CAMPAIGN ONE "OPERATION MAXIMUM OVERKILL",
# MISSION 5 OF 10 -- {Night of Death}* [MIS].
# Spec, provenance and every open question: mods/comanche/doc/campaign.md, terrain.md,
# substitutions.md, hud.md. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md.
#
# THE TASK [MIS]: THREE goals out of 29 objects. "Several key missile sites that we would like to
# have removed" -- three starred Geckos, and 26 objects that must not enter the verdict.
#
# THE FIELD [MIS]: map 3 (Ka'u Desert, Hawaii, terrain.md 6), night -- sun -83.05 deg at the
# lead's spawn, computed by the runner. 3 starred objects, unlock marker *.
# THE CAST: 9 Werewolf -> `ah64` - 7 T-80 -> `target_hard` - 1 fuel tank -> `target_soft` - 11
# Gecko -> `sa8` - wingman -> `f16`.
# THE LOADOUT [MIS]: cannon 500, rockets 62, Hellfire 8, Stinger 8, artillery 2, wingman 12, fuel
# 12000. Declared here: 4 x `mk82`, 4 x `aim9`, gun 500, `set fuel_int_pct 60` = 12000 against the
# campaign's own maximum of 20 000. The rockets and the artillery have no row and no mechanism;
# the truncation of the other two is the F-16's nine pylons.

# ---- THE SEVEN DISCLOSURES ARE STATED IN FULL IN c01m01-werewolves-on-patrol.fbm AND APPLY HERE
# ---- UNCHANGED: D1 no rotorcraft (the RAH-66 flies as `module f16`, 300 kt because 180-275 kt crash
# ---- the egress) - D2 the Werewolf is an `ah64` mover and fires nothing, ever - D3 flat 0 m ground,
# ---- because one mod carries one DEM and this campaign needs four theatres - D4 the clock is checked
# ---- against the logged sun elevation - D5 the anchoring is terrain.md's reconstruction and the
# ---- campaign names no place - D6 the striker spawns on the bearing to its aim point, because the
# ---- attack phase cannot fly itself onto its own run-in - D7 one striker is one aim point.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `lead`'s.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 requires the 3 starred Geckos and nothing else. 26 of the 29 objects are irrelevant
#   to the verdict and MUST NOT enter it; a run that clears the map and leaves one missile site
#   standing is a FAIL. This is the campaign's smallest goal set and therefore the only mission whose
#   goal set is inside D7's reach at all -- read the met count against 3, not against 29.
#   exit 3 = the expected reading.

# MEASURED (exit 3, `--elev const`): TWO OF THREE -- the campaign's best result, and the only file
#   whose goal set is small enough for D7 not to decide it.
#   t = 21.4 / 24.6 s   two Mk-82 away, aimErrM 12.48 and 8.81; g01 and g02 destroyed
#   verdict             `lead` TIMEOUT, 2 of 3 met, `survive` met; `two` SUCCESS. 54 SA-8 launches --
#                       the campaign's heaviest -- closest 209.91 m, no hit. The third site, g03, is
#                       simply never attacked: there is no third striker and no second pass.

unit lead
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight m05 1
  spawn 19.39619 -155.30258 150 103.0 300
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 60
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 4 mk82
  set store 6 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim9
  set store 8 aim9
  set store 9 aim9
  set gun_rounds 500
  set cmds_mode auto
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 19.38746 -155.26257 150 300
  wp 19.37979 -155.22741 1000 300
  objective kill unit g01
  objective kill unit g02
  objective kill unit g03
  objective survive

